  "reason": "The records collectively make the later result plausibly reconstructible. R9 and R17 establish SPS near 1000–1050 °C for Co/Fe/Ti-containing high-entropy alloys, while R2, R5, R7, R14, and R19 establish SPS consolidation of mechanically alloyed or ball-milled BCC refractory/high-entropy powders, including densification and oxide or second-phase precipitation. R2 and R7 additionally show that changing SPS temperature alters diffusion, secondary phases, and passivation. Separately, R1, R3, R4, R11, and R16 directly connect dense, uniform oxide/passive films with inhibited oxygen or ionic penetration and improved oxidation and chloride-corrosion resistance. Thus an expert could combine SPS near 1000 °C with diffusion-enabled densification and distributed oxide barriers to propose the later mechanism. The exact MgAlTiVFeCo composition, specific AlV2O4/FeAl2O4/FeTiO3 phases, quantitative optimum, and biphasic parabolic oxidation kinetics are not disclosed, but they are refinements rather than a wholly new intervention concept."
